{"runId": "run_md_0001", "seq": 7, "kind": "interrupt", "at": "2026-11-18T09:33:00Z", "release": "feature-development@1.3.0", "node": "approve_plan", "attempt": 1, "interrupt": {"interruptId": "int_run_md_0001_approve_plan_1", "stage": "plan", "message": "Brainstorming, round 1: answer the questions with **Request changes**, or **Approve** to let the agent decide the rest.", "plan": "QUESTIONS:\n\nThe repo has an `orders` module but no discount logic yet. Two choices decide the shape of the change.\n\n### Discount model\n1. **Where do discounts live?** (a) per order line; (b) per order; (c) both. **I'd pick (a).** It keeps `total == sum(lines)` a one-line invariant.\n2. **Rounding:** `Decimal` with `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, rounded per line. **Agree?**\n\n### Limits\n| Rule | Proposal | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| Max discount | 100 % | a line can be free, never negative |\n| Stacking | not allowed | one code per line keeps the audit simple |\n| Currency | order currency only | no FX in this change |\n\n### Out of scope\n- [x] coupon codes UI\n- [ ] ~~loyalty points~~ (later milestone)\n\n> Answer with **Request changes** (one line per question is enough), or **Approve** to let me decide the rest."}}
